To prevent BGP routes from being reflected back to members of the same neighbor group while maintaining proper route distribution, enable split-horizon at the group level:

```
configure router bgp group "RR-CLIENTS" split-horizon
```

**Explanation:**  
- `split-horizon` ensures routes received from a peer in the group are not reflected back to any peer in the same group.  
- This applies to all address families and peer types (IBGP/EBGP).  
- Replace `"RR-CLIENTS"` with your actual BGP group name.  

**Verification:**  
After applying, check that routes from group members are no longer reflected to peers within the group using:  
```
show router bgp group "RR-CLIENTS"
```

> **Note:**  
> - The command takes effect immediately without requiring a BGP session reset.  
> - For granular control per neighbor, apply `split-horizon` at the neighbor level instead.  
> - Avoid `disable-client-reflect` as it blocks all route reflection to the group, breaking required path distribution.
