## User question:
During a core network expansion project where we're expecting a significant influx of new BGP peers, what's the proper method to adjust session capacity limits on our Nokia 7750 SR routers? Specifically, I need to ensure the existing BGP instance can handle up to 500 dynamically established neighbor relationships without impacting current peering stability.
---
## Proposed answer:
To adjust the BGP session capacity for up to 500 dynamic peers on your Nokia 7750 SR router, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    dynamic-neighbor-limit 500
exit
```

This command sets the instance-wide limit for dynamic BGP sessions to 500, ensuring the router accepts new peer connections without impacting existing sessions. If dynamic peers are grouped, also configure the group-specific limit:

```cli
configure router bgp group "GROUP_NAME"
    dynamic-neighbor
        prefix <ip-prefix/prefix-length>
    exit
    dynamic-neighbor-limit 500
exit
```

Replace `GROUP_NAME` with your peer group name and `<ip-prefix/prefix-length>` with the subnet from which dynamic peers connect. This ensures session limits apply consistently at both instance and group levels.
