To address the BGP next-hop resolution issues for labeled IPv4 routes in your MPLS transport network, configure tunnel-based resolution under BGP next-hop settings:

```cli
/configure router bgp next-hop-resolution
    labeled-routes
        transport-tunnel
            family ipv4
                resolution any
```

This configuration enables BGP to resolve next-hops using any supported MPLS tunnel type (LDP, RSVP, SR, etc.) while maintaining your existing label distribution policies. The `resolution any` directive follows the Tunnel Table Manager's (TTM) default preference order for tunnel selection. 

For VPN-IPv4 route resolution enhancement on route reflectors, add:
```cli
/configure router bgp 
    enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
```

The first command sequence ensures all labeled IPv4 routes (including labeled unicast and VPN-IP) use MPLS tunnels for next-hop resolution. The second command optimizes VPN route handling in route reflector scenarios by enabling next-hop resolution in a dedicated VRF context.
