To configure your Nokia 7750 SR routers to exchange only a single best path per prefix for labeled-unicast IPv4 routes, use the following CLI commands. This ensures only one path is advertised and received per prefix without impacting existing route propagation:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "group-name"
        add-paths
            label-ipv4 send 1 receive none
```

**Key details:**
- Apply this under the relevant BGP group or neighbor context. Replace `"group-name"` with your peer group name.
- `send 1` restricts path advertisements to a maximum of one best path per prefix.
- `receive none` prevents the router from accepting multiple paths per prefix from peers.
- This configuration is specific to `label-ipv4` (labeled-unicast IPv4). Adjust for other address families if needed using analogous commands.
