To selectively filter BGP paths and ensure only desired routes are installed in the default instance, configure the `resolution-filter` command under BGP next-hop resolution for IPv4 and IPv6 families. This controls which tunnel types can resolve unlabeled BGP routes, preventing unintended programming into the routing table and forwarding database. For example, to restrict resolution to RSVP and SR-ISIS tunnels:

```cli
configure router bgp next-hop-res shortcut-tunn family ipv4
    resolution-filter rsvp sr-isis
exit
configure router bgp next-hop-res shortcut-tunn family ipv6
    resolution-filter rsvp sr-isis
exit
```

For labeled BGP paths, use BGP import policies (not covered in the reference) to explicitly control route acceptance and installation.
