To selectively advertise the default route (0.0.0.0/0) only to specific downstream peers via BGP on the Nokia 7750 SR, use the `default-route-target` command applied directly to the desired BGP neighbors or groups. This ensures the default route is originated and advertised exclusively to the configured peers without propagation throughout the entire AS.

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <target-group-name>
        family ipv4
        neighbor <downstream-peer-ip>
            default-route-target
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- Replace `<target-group-name>` with the BGP group containing the downstream peers.  
- Replace `<downstream-peer-ip>` with the IP addresses of the specific peers that should receive the default route.  
- The `default-route-target` command originates the default route (0.0.0.0/0) and restricts its advertisement to only the configured peers.  
- This configuration is applied at the neighbor level for granular control, ensuring no unintended propagation to other BGP peers.
