To ensure proper handling of orphaned VPN-IPv4 and VPN-IPv6 routes not associated with any VPRN instances, configure the BGP next-hop resolution to use a dummy VRF for route import and resolution. Enable the resolution for VPN routes and specify acceptable transport tunnel types:

```
configure router bgp
    enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family vpn
                    resolution-filter
                        ldp true
                        rsvp true
                        sr-isis true
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `enable-rr-vpn-forwarding` imports all received VPN routes into a dummy VRF for next-hop resolution.  
- Under `family vpn`, the `resolution-filter` specifies which tunnel types (e.g., LDP, RSVP, SR-ISIS) are eligible to resolve next-hops for orphaned VPN routes. Adjust tunnel types (`ldp`, `rsvp`, `sr-isis`) based on your transport infrastructure.
