To ensure graceful restarts during maintenance without triggering unnecessary route withdrawals, configure the following on your Nokia 7750 SR:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        restart-time 300
        stale-routes-time 300
        long-lived
            forwarding-bits-set all
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `graceful-restart` enables BGP helper functionality to preserve adjacencies during neighbor restarts.  
- `restart-time 300` sets the maximum time peers will wait for this router to re-establish after a restart (default: 300 seconds).  
- `stale-routes-time 300` maintains received routes for 300 seconds during peer restarts to prevent immediate route flushing.  
- `forwarding-bits-set all` ensures the F-bit is advertised for all address families, signaling preserved forwarding state across restarts.  

This configuration maintains forwarding state during peer reboots and prevents unnecessary BGP route recalculations.
